From: mi8 <mi8@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mi8-0188: do not inherit CS_RESTRICT

dyld discards DYLD_* for a process that carries it, and a platform binary's
signature does. The hakios kernel never marks these binaries as platform ones and
so never has the flag; this port does, hence one line removed from the mask that
exec inherits.

---
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -1387,7 +1387,7 @@
 	if (load_result.csflags & CS_VALID) {
 		imgp->ip_csflags |= load_result.csflags &
 		    (CS_VALID | CS_SIGNED | CS_DEV_CODE | CS_LINKER_SIGNED |
-		    CS_HARD | CS_KILL | CS_RESTRICT | CS_ENFORCEMENT | CS_REQUIRE_LV |
+		    CS_HARD | CS_KILL | CS_ENFORCEMENT | CS_REQUIRE_LV |
 		    CS_FORCED_LV | CS_ENTITLEMENTS_VALIDATED | CS_NO_UNTRUSTED_HELPERS | CS_RUNTIME |
 		    CS_ENTITLEMENT_FLAGS |
 		    CS_EXEC_SET_HARD | CS_EXEC_SET_KILL | CS_EXEC_SET_ENFORCEMENT);
